pagewire's change to PAPPL v1.4.12: answer Disable-Printer, Enable-Printer
and Cancel-Current-Job only for local clients.

Upstream these three operations authorize through _papplPrinterIsAuthorized(),
which calls _papplClientIsAuthorizedForGroup() with allow_remote=true. With no
auth service, every client may then stop a queue accepting jobs, start it
again, or cancel the job that is printing. That is how the retrofit Printer
Applications run in pagewire, and they listen on every address of the node.

With this patch the three use papplClientIsAuthorized() like Pause-Printer:
loopback or the domain socket only, or an authenticated client when an auth
service is set. Cancel-Current-Job checks before it looks for the job, so a
remote client gets 403 whether or not a job is printing. Job operations
(Print-Job, Create-Job, Send-Document, Validate-Job, Get-Jobs,
Get-Job-Attributes, Cancel-Job, Hold-Job, Release-Job, Close-Job) and
subscriptions are unchanged.

